[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ The pain [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhat does "debug production issues" mean concretely — what can't you see today?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mErrors vanish silently[39m
     [38;5;246mSomething fails for a real user and you never hear about it. You need failures reported back to you, not sitting in
[39m     [38;5;246ma browser console nobody reads.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Can't reconstruct a session
     [38;5;246mYou hear about a bug but can't retrace what the user did. You need an ordered trail of events with enough context [39m
     [38;5;246mto replay the path.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Logs exist but are unusable
     [38;5;246mOutput is there but unstructured, unfiltered, and un-searchable. You need levels, structure, and the ability to [39m
     [38;5;246mturn verbosity up or down.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m No specific incident yet
     [38;5;246mNothing is on fire — you want the instrumentation in place before it is. Design for general readiness rather than a
[39m     [38;5;246mknown failure.[39m
